# In-repo Python venv for the vendored speech backend (created via
# `python -m venv venv` + `pip install -r src/speech/requirements.txt`).
# Heavy + machine-specific — NEVER commit. The code lives in src/speech/ (tracked).
venv/
# (MIT, upstream jamiepine/voicebox, vendored 2026-07-20 commit 52f8d8d).
# Runtime artifacts inside it are excluded via src/speech/.gitignore.
# Regenerated by scripts/vendor-real-voice-backend.mjs from /c/one/voicebox.

# Vendored backend RUNTIME DATA (sqlite db, profiles, generated audio cache).
# The speech backend writes its data dir relative to cwd (src/), which would
# create src/data/voicebox.db. We redirect it via VOICEBOX_DATA_DIR to a
# gitignored cache path, but ignore the leak too as defense-in-depth.
src/data/
*.db
voicebox.db

# Python (bytecode, caches, virtualenvs) — regenerable, machine-specific
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/



